.TH REM_DEVELOPER_GUIDE 7 "September 2026" "REM developer tools" "Miscellaneous Information"
.SH NAME
REM_DEVELOPER_GUIDE \- offline REM development handbook
.SH DESCRIPTION
The REM developer handbook covers first login, project layout, C and
assembly builds, Make and Samurai, native tools, remdbg, examples, and
recovery. The Markdown guide is installed as
.I /usr/share/doc/rem/REM_DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md .
.PP
The handbook is a navigation and workflow guide. Consult the linked ABI,
syscall, linker, compiler, and qualification documents for current details.
Image contents and acceptance are image-specific.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/rem/examples
Offline source examples.
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1
Command pages for chibicc, remdbg, and samu.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chibicc (1),
.BR remdbg (1),
.BR samu (1)
